.fi
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
.bd
Stty
sets the status of the character device named by
.bd
descriptor
from the six-byte
.bd
struct sgtty
pointed at by
.bd
vec.
The structure is the one
.bd
gtty
(3) returns, and its fields - the two speeds, the erase and
kill characters, and the mode word - are described there.
.sp
It is the request
.bd
TIOCSETA
through
.bd
ioctl
(2), so it may be made to any character device; a device
whose status cannot be set answers ENOTTY.  Turning echo
off for a password is the usual use: get the block with
.bd
gtty ,
clear the echo bit, and set it back with
.bd
stty .
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
0 on success, -1 on failure.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
ERRORS
.in +5
.br
.bd
EBADF
if descriptor is not an open file.
.br
.bd
ENOTTY
if it does not name a character device, or the device has no
settable terminal status.
